Z||000000||GT Bastard||02-12-2000||03:23 PM||||Do the '15 crosslaced rims on a GT mean the car is equipped with WS6?  Or was WS6 standard on all GT's?<P>This page made me wonder: <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/mt/fierotech/v800/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/mt/fierotech/v800/index.html</A> <BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||HF6582||02-12-2000||03:49 PM||||On my 86GT it does not have WS6 on the suspension. I thought that maybe it did but I looked at the option codes and it doesn't.<P>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||02-12-2000||03:51 PM||||It was standard on the GT and the Formula and optional on the SE and Sport Coupe. WS-6 denoted different tuned shocks/struts, bigger sway bar, (Rear swaybar in 88) and stiffer springs. Some of the early SEs had 14 inch wheels AND had WS-6 option.<P>A GT without WS-6??? Never heard of such a beast! Sounds like a GT without a V6!<P>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 02-12-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 02-12-2000).]||||reg||1
